  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-14, in chat): \"when editing a slot without making a selection, the A/B X/Y coordinaes should update int he viewport in realtime. And the settings for manually defining a slot should live under its own section rather than under Selection.. section should be called manual.\"\n\nWhat happens:\n- The user edits a Slot operation that has no selection and changes the X or Y coordinate of point A or point B. The viewport does not show the change while the user edits.\n- The fields that define a slot by hand are in the \"Selection\" section.\n\nExpected:\n- The viewport shows points A and B and the slot line between them. The preview follows each edit of the A and B coordinates immediately.\n- The fields that define a slot by hand are in their own section. The name of the section is \"Manual\".\n\nNotes: the preview is ephemeral UI state. The committed coordinate edit stays an undoable command. The posted program does not change.\n\nDone means: a structural UI test pins the \"Manual\" section and its fields, and that \"Selection\" no longer contains them; a test pins that the preview geometry follows an edit of the A or B coordinates before the edit is committed; the PR description has before and after screenshots.\n",
